{"id":"u-c5492fb5-b1a3-4bbe-8522-7649e0be144e","src":"community","title":"Classic Physique: Phase 2 by Beverly International","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/nrUVU5-beverly-international-classic-physique","desc":"Train three days on – one day off: \n\nDay 1: Chest and Back\nDay 2: Legs\nDay 3: Shoulders and Arms\nDay 4: Off; Repeat\n\nDuring Phase 2 training you’ll be doing a lot of supersets. Supersets allow you to get more work done in less time. Remember, less rest between sets is one of the parameters of progress. Your Phase 2 training will be more focused on improving your proportions and increasing your chest to waist ratio.\n\nAs your diet becomes stricter during phase 2, it will become harder and harder to increase reps or poundage, so reducing the time between sets becomes more and more important. You’ll be supersetting antagonistic muscle groups to improve balance and proportion as well as to add a fat burning aspect to your training.\n\nIt’s not necessary to “run” from one exercise to the next when supersetting. After you complete a superset rest 60-90 seconds and then start your next set. Since you will be working each bodypart twice every eight days, we will no longer be performing feeder workouts.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-01T15:17:40.699Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest, Back, & Abs","Legs & Calves","Shoulders, Arms, & Abs","Conditioning","Chest, Back, & Abs","Legs & Calves","Shoulders, Arms, & Abs"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Chin-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":7,"x":4}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Pec Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe"